## Original Content
Les Forces démocratiques syriennes, dont le chef Mazloum Abdi a annoncé, mardi, la dissolution en vertu d'un accord avec le président Ahmed al-Charaa, constituaient l'armée des Kurdes de Syrie et avaient vaincu avec le soutien de l'Occident les jihadistes du groupe État islamique.

## Summary
The Syrian Democratic Forces (SDF) announced their dissolution following an agreement with President Ahmed al-Charaa. The SDF was the Kurdish army in Syria and had previously defeated Islamic State jihadists with Western support.

## Key Points
- The Syrian Democratic Forces have dissolved as part of an agreement with Ahmed al-Charaa.
- The dissolution was announced by Mazloum Abdi, the chief of the SDF.
- The SDF played a key role in defeating Islamic State jihadists with Western backing.
- This event marks a significant change in the regional military and political landscape.


